  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nAn upper ridge over Montana will be flattened by an upper low that\nmoves east from the Gulf of Alaska over the next several days.\nSouthwest upper flow combined with prefrontal compressional\nheating will send the mercury above 100 for a lot of real estate\nfrom central to eastern Montana. Some locations likely to\nchallenge daily high temperature records. An Excessive Heat\nWarning is in effect from noon today through noon Sunday for the\nwestern zones and till 6 pm Sunday for the eastern zones. \n\nIncreasing south winds will give rise to fire weather concerns as\nthe sun shouldn/t have too many clouds to fight with. Only \nmorning smoke would inhibit it and that should disperse during the\nday. A Red Flag Warning is in effect from 2 PM this afternoon to \n9 PM MDT Sunday.\n\nThe strong upper low will send a couple cold fronts southeast\nacross the area, the first one arriving about midnight tonight\nwith the second pushing through Monday morning. Wind will signal\ntheir arrival as only small chances of brief showers are \nexpected. A Lake Wind Advisory is effect tonight through Sunday\nthat will likely need an extension through Monday.\n\nAfter Monday, the upper trough moves east and a zonal flow\nsuccumbs a bit to a Desert southwest ridge by the end of the\nforecast cycle. Expect dry conditions with temperatures warming to\nnear normal. Winds generally look light so Fire Weather issues\nshould be minimal.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nBase forecast elements were not changed as NBM seemed to be \nhandling most elements well. However CAMS could provide more\ndetail later today.\n\nTFJ",
